WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.457
Security detections are not one-time rules that remain useful forever.

00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:08.379
They depend on telemetry, environments, threat behavior, analyst workflows,

00:00:08.379 --> 00:00:09.686
and business context.

00:00:09.686 --> 00:00:13.608
Detection lifecycle management treats detections as living defensive assets.

00:00:13.608 --> 00:00:18.837
Each detection should have a purpose, owner, data source, expected behavior, documentation,

00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:21.016
review process, and improvement path.

00:00:21.016 --> 00:00:25.809
Without lifecycle management, detections can become noisy, outdated, duplicated, or ignored.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:31.474
A rule that once produced useful signal may lose value as systems, users,

00:00:31.474 --> 00:00:32.781
and threats change.

00:00:32.781 --> 00:00:38.010
The lifecycle mindset helps teams maintain a reliable portfolio of signals instead

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.060
of a growing folder of unmanaged rules.
